# Invite links are /invite/<one-time-token>. On a device with the app installed
# iOS intercepts these as universal links and this page is never fetched; the
# rewrite is the fallback for everyone else (Android, desktop, app not yet
# installed), serving one landing page for any token.
#
# Status 200 makes this a REWRITE, not a redirect — deliberate, since a 3xx on
# an invite URL would break the universal-link handoff.
#
# The destination deliberately lives OUTSIDE /invite/. Pointing it at
# /invite/index.html made the target match the /invite/* pattern itself, which
# Cloudflare drops as a possible rewrite loop — the rule silently never applied
# and every token fell through to the homepage.
/invite/*  /invite-landing.html  200
